<div class="c"><h1 class="redstar">Poetry By:Misti</h1></div><h2 class="c">Microcosm</h2><p>I no longer believe in loneliness<br> (hesitating little lies we tell<br>to pretend we aren't afraid.)<br>And I no longer believe in fear<br>(excuses made to keep us from our laziness <br>at trying something new.)<br><br>No, I no longer believe in <br>your mantras (slowly worked <br>a chasm <br>into my passionate belief in life)<br><br>Now<br><br> as I claw out. <br>bleeding, dirt caked fingernails<br>hang onto the earth-<br>and I believe in that earth<br>which chokes <br>burns<br>tastes like salty bitter death<br>on my lips~E<br>...and pain in every limb<br>as I creep ever steadily forward<br>....upward.......<br>I believe in that pain<br>a sweet burning  death<br>once dulled by every kiss you gave.<br><br>I am not lonely or afraid<br>without you.<br>I am not strong<br>Or brave.<br><br>I am a microcosm<br>A little universe of possibility.<br>A woman fully aware of desirability<br>and grass and sky and cool lapping water<br>around ankles when I'm not conscious<br>of falling in love....<br><br>But it's there in the ripples of the tide<br>As I drown and resurface....<br>..........I drown and resurface.....<br>.............drown and resurface...........<br>..........................................resurface............<br>because I choose to suffer<br>rather than bear your numb cross<br>of safe and secluded dreams.<br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"><h2 class="c">Weeping Widow</h2><p>Quivering<br>I watch the vast flowing tendrils<br>of the weeping willow<br>race the wind toward the lake.<br>My wavering hands follow <br>the patterns of her dark and bony roots <br>which lie deep and strong.<br><br>Bound to our earth,<br>she may not drown into the shadows<br>of the cool muddy water;<br>but must witness shards of lightning<br>burn wicked nightmares in this storm.<br>As I huddle beneath her,<br>she shall dance<br>against the pelting drops of rain<br>her strands twisted in their shivering;<br>fear inaudible within this tempest.<br><br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"><h2 class="c">Sly Park, Audust 1998</h2><p>You are tangled indecision<br>your desire<br>   your displeasure<br>       splinter me<br>into a mass of shattered pieces.<br><br>Hang your knots<br>upon twisted bony roots <br>raw and exposed<br>by those little whispering echoes<br>of your hesitancy <br>         blowing<br>             through<br>                    my hair.<br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"><h2 class="c">Photographs</h2><p><br>            The light is my lover.<br>She is my depth,<br>          my focus.<br>    Even<br>        in the deepest shadows,<br>            the corners of dim hallways,<br>    or the sprawling shade of an oak,<br>                     her shifting patterns emerge<br>           to taunt me.<br>I linger <br>  to witness her explosion <br> against the horizon, <br>          struggling to capture her reflections<br>   upon the cool marble headstone<br>hoping to become wise to her changing temperaments.<br>           But she is eternal<br>            wiser than my amateur eyes.<br><br><br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"></body>
